---
// Served as /privacy.html (build.format "preserve"). Google's OAuth consent
// screen links to that exact URL: do not move or rename this page.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What Heracles Records reads, where it keeps it, and what it sends to the services you choose to connect."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Effective 4 October 2026</p>

    <p>
      Heracles Records is a desktop app that runs on your computer. It has no accounts of its
      own, and its developer runs no servers: nothing you do in the app is sent to the
      developer. This policy explains what the app reads, where it keeps it, and what it sends
      to the services you choose to connect.
    </p>

    <h2>Google user data</h2>
    <p>
      Connecting Google Drive is optional. It is used only for Sync, which keeps your Heracles
      Records data the same on each of your own computers.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>What the app can access.</strong> The app asks only for the
        <code>drive.file</code> permission. It creates one folder named
        <em>Heracles Records</em> in your Drive and can read and change only the files it
        created there. It cannot see or change any other file in your Drive.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>What it stores there.</strong> Your coach conversations, training plans, app
        preferences and the change log Sync needs to merge your computers. These files are
        scrambled with a key built into the app, which keeps them out of Drive previews and
        search; it is not encryption against someone with access to your Drive.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>What it reads about your account.</strong> The email address, name and storage
        use of the connected Google account, to show which account Sync is using.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Where your sign-in is kept.</strong> The Google sign-in token is stored only on
        your computer, encrypted with your operating system's secure storage. It is never sent
        anywhere except to Google.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sharing.</strong> Google user data is not sold, not shared with anyone, not used
        for advertising, and not used to train AI models. It moves only between your computer
        and your own Google Drive.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Stopping and deleting.</strong> Disconnect Google Drive in the app under
        Settings → Sync, or remove the app's access at
        <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>.
        To delete what Sync stored, delete the <em>Heracles Records</em> folder from your Drive.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Heracles Records' use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to
      the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy"
        >Google API Services User Data Policy</a
      >, including the Limited Use requirements.
    </p>

    <h2>Data on your computer</h2>
    <p>
      Your training data, conversations, plans and settings are stored in the app's data folder
      on your computer. Passwords, keys and sign-in tokens are encrypted with your operating
      system's secure storage where it is available. Uninstalling the app and deleting its data
      folder removes them.
    </p>

    <h2>Services you connect</h2>
    <p>
      When you connect a service, the app talks to it directly from your computer, and that
      service's own privacy policy applies:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>COROS:</strong> your activities, sleep, plans, workouts and calendar, read and
        saved with your COROS account.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>AI providers</strong> you choose for the coach (such as OpenAI, Anthropic,
        OpenRouter, or a model on your own computer): your questions and the training data the
        coach needs to answer them. Each conversation reads only the data you allow it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Hevy:</strong> the strength workouts you import, read with your Hevy API key.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Maps and place names:</strong> map images from map providers (OpenFreeMap,
        OpenStreetMap, OpenTopoMap, CyclOSM, Esri), and the approximate location of places you
        trained, rounded to about a kilometre, sent to OpenStreetMap's Nominatim or Photon to
        name them.
      </li>
      <li><strong>GitHub:</strong> checking for and downloading app updates.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>The app contains no analytics, tracking or crash reporting.</p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      This website sets no cookies and contains no analytics or tracking. It is hosted on
      GitHub Pages; GitHub receives the technical details any web host does, such as your IP
      address, under the
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
        >GitHub General Privacy Statement</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the new version will be published on this page with a new
      effective date.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy: open an issue at
      <a href="https://github.com/quochungse/HeraclesRecords/issues"
        >github.com/quochungse/HeraclesRecords/issues</a
      >.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
